# ---- Vendored assets: kits imported at these paths stay machine-local ----
#
# NOTE, because the rules below no longer tell the whole story: the project DOES
# commit its Asset Store kits, at Assets/_COREHOLD/Vendored/Vendor/ — a path
# none of these patterns match. That was deliberate (builds have to work from a
# clone) and it is load-bearing: 49 committed assets reference 525 vendor GUIDs,
# so those kits cannot be dropped without gutting a fresh checkout. They are
# stored via Git LFS — see .gitattributes and docs/git_lfs_migration.md.
#
# What these rules still do is keep a kit imported to the DEFAULT Asset Store
# location out of the repo, so importing a package to try it does not commit it.
# Promote a kit deliberately by moving it under _COREHOLD/Vendored/, or copy just
# what a scene needs into a committed _COREHOLD folder (the Skin From Kit tool
# does this for UI sprites) — half-imported kits are the dangling-GUID trap.
/[Aa]ssets/Vendor/
/[Aa]ssets/Vendor.meta
/[Aa]ssets/Yoge/
/[Aa]ssets/Yoge.meta
/[Aa]ssets/Layer Lab/
/[Aa]ssets/Layer Lab.meta
/[Aa]ssets/Eric VFX Studio/
/[Aa]ssets/Eric VFX Studio.meta
/[Aa]ssets/Free Slash VFX/
/[Aa]ssets/Free Slash VFX.meta
/[Aa]ssets/_Recovery/
/[Aa]ssets/_Recovery.meta

